# Cross-frame fault propagation (error-model.md §11, Increment 2.1a): an overflow
# raised INSIDE a callee (`faulty`) propagates to a `catch Fault.Overflow` in its
# DIRECT caller (`main`), without unwind — the callee writes a fault tag into a
# hidden trailing slot, and the caller branches to the handler before reading the
# result. Expected stdout: -1 (the handler value), NOT a panic.
int faulty(int a, int b): a * b           # may overflow; NO local catch

void main():
    int big = 4611686018427387904         # 2^62; 2^62 * 2^62 overflows i64
    int r = faulty(big, big) catch Fault.Overflow: -1
    print(f"{r}")
